# Oakhaven (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, section 3): the Warmwood. Slow, rooted, warm; trees, roots, bark and shade.
# Drafts (phase 3), to be written properly with you (phase 7).

grammar oakhaven
greet = Shade on you | Good shade
greet.broad = Shade an' shelter
farewell = Root well | Shade keep you
agree = Rooted true | Aye, that
refuse = That won't take root
surprise = Leaf and limb | Well, branch me
annoyed = Blight it | Knots and knots
very = proper
good = good bark | sound wood
bad = rotten | windthrown
worthless = deadwood
luck = good growing weather
child = sapling
pet!! = acorn | my sapling
tired = felled
nonsense = sawdust
tag = , mm?
oath! = Bark and branch | Old Oak | Root and rain
home = under my own roof-beam
# (Phase 7, the rest of plain's words.)
address = old root | friend
address[other.stage=young] = sapling | young 'un
bed = my pallet | the bough-bed
cold = nippy | cold as a stump
dear! = my oak | my heartwood | love
drunk = sap-soaked | mellow
hot = close under the leaves | sultry
hungry = hollow as a log | hungry
hurt = barked | sore
little = a twig | a little
money = coin | acorns
rain = drip | leaf-rain
robbery = Rank robbery, that | Stripped bare, like beetles had been at it
saying! = Slow grows the oak | Every tree falls in its season | Roots first, then branches
thanks = Thank you kindly | Bless you
work = the cutting | the work
# (Phase 7, the conversations' words.)
wages = pay | coin
boss = the old oak | the master
busy = at it root and branch | busy
slow = slow as sap | quiet
cheated = barked | done
mum! = Mam | Mother
dad! = Da | Father
gran = Granny | Old Mother
grandad = Grandsire | Old Father
supper = supper | the pot
toffs = the city folk | the polished lot
busybody = magpie | gossip
fool = you great stump | you knot-head
daft = woodwormed | daft
toast = Deep roots | Good shade | Sap rise
drink = a cup of perry | a jar
fog = mist in the trees | fog
wind = wind in the tops | a blow
ale = acorn ale | ale
thief = nut-robber | thief
bandits = wood-robbers | bandits
grave = under the roots | the ground
grub = victuals | grub
snug = snug as a squirrel | cosy
poorly = drooping | poorly
remedy = willow bark | a moss poultice | elder syrup
olddays = the old growth | days gone by
blessing = Shade keep you | Root well | Good growing to you
bless = Shade keep you | Root and keep you
someday = some green year | one day
far = through the wood and out | a long walk
stranger = outlander | stranger
